Step 1 — Create tracking fields on Transfers (stock.picking)

We’ll add four fields that power the button logic and audit trail.
==================================================================
1A) Open Studio on the Transfer form

Go to Inventory → Operations → Transfers.

Open any Handoff transfer (or any transfer—just for editing the view).

Click ⋮ (gear) → Studio to open Studio on the transfer form.
==================================================================
1B) Add fields (all on model: Transfer (stock.picking))

Create these four fields:

Pickup Notified

Type: Boolean

Technical name: x_ready_notified

Label: Pickup Notified

Properties: set Read-only (we’ll update it via server action)

Placement: put this in a small “Notifications” section on the form (not the header).

Pickup Notified On

Type: Datetime

Technical name: x_ready_notified_on

Label: Pickup Notified On

Properties: Read-only

Placement: same “Notifications” section.

Pickup Notified By

Type: Many2one → Users (res.users)

Technical name: x_ready_notified_by

Label: Pickup Notified By

Properties: Read-only

Placement: same “Notifications” section.

Notify Count

Type: Integer

Technical name: x_notify_count

Label: Notify Count

Widget: Badge (in field options → Widget → choose Badge)

Properties: Read-only

Placement: drag this field into the header (top bar of the form) to the right side so users see it like a counter next to the future button.

Tip: If “Badge” isn’t available in your Studio widget list, leave it as an Integer for now—we’ll still increment it; we can change the widget later.
==================================================================
B1) Add the partner field (Studio → Contacts)

Open Contacts → any partner → Studio.

Add a Text field:

Label: Pickup extra emails

Technical name: x_pickup_extra_emails

Help text: “Comma/semicolon/space separated emails to notify when orders are ready for pickup.”
